# Repo-root build context (all Dockerfiles use `context: .`).
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.pdf
**/*.pdf
docs
notes
supabase
scripts/demo

# Secrets for the api and admin panel are supplied at RUNTIME through
# docker-compose `env_file`, so they must not be baked into image layers.
apps/api/.env
apps/api/.env.*
!apps/api/.env.example

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED either: apps/admin-panel/.env.local. `next build`
# collects page data for /export/clients, which imports a module that reads
# DATABASE_URL at import time, so the build fails without it. Baking it into the
# image is the pre-existing behaviour; removing that needs those routes to be
# force-dynamic and the env read deferred to request time.

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: apps/web/.env.local* — the web image build bakes
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values from it (apps/web/Dockerfile COPYs it).
